            "heading": "Why you sweat.",
            "text": "<p>Sweat is how your body cools down. As it evaporates from your skin, it carries heat away with it.</p><p>How much you sweat depends on how hard you train, how hot and humid it is, your size and your genetics. During hard exercise, sweat rates commonly run between half a litre and two litres an hour, and more in the heat.</p>",
