          "settings": {
            "heading": "What's in sweat.",
            "text": "<p>Sweat is mostly water, but it also carries electrolytes out of your body. Sodium is the main one. Potassium and magnesium are lost too, in much smaller amounts.</p><p>How salty your sweat is varies a lot from person to person. For most people it's somewhere between about 460 and 1,840 mg of sodium per litre. If you get white salt marks on your kit or stinging eyes, you're probably at the saltier end.</p>",
            "stat": "460\u20131,840 mg",
